A||||19||bpfiero||weight reduction???||||5||
Z||000000||bpfiero||06-06-2001||12:46 AM||||Hey people.... quick question,  does anybody have any knowledge about weight reduction in a fiero,  what you can and/or can't take off, cut off, or replace?? I'm sure someone out there has looked into it or tried to lighten the load a bit.   <BR> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||pontiacs4me||06-06-2001||01:14 AM||||If you dont care about being comfortable in the summer, take out all of the ac stuff.  I havent ever owned a car with ac, so why start now?  I pulled everything from the compressor and lines to the condenser and everything probably weighs a hundred pounds.  Take out the carpet, and remove the sound deadner, use lightweight racing buckets, take out the spare in the front.  You can probably knock it down 300 lbs total before you start making it unsafe.  (dont even think of swiss cheesing the space frame)||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||06-06-2001||01:15 AM||||HUMMMMM &gt; &gt; &gt; &gt; &gt;...........<BR>How about ........&gt;<BR>SLIM FAST? ? ? ?  ?&gt;&lt;&gt;&lt;&gt;&lt;&gt;&lt;&gt;&lt;<P>LOL  ||||reg||12
Z||000003||mrgone||06-06-2001||04:24 AM||||yeah i just took out the spare tire<P>man that thing was heavy<P>moved all trunk contents (loose oil water and coolent bottles) up to its place, am ripping out the sound insulation on the sides of the engine, leaving the firewall alone. thats about all im gonna do for now<P>that winshield washer fluid container is huge! i just dumped 2L into the thing when it was about 1/3 full||||reg||1
