Z||000011||danny boy||06-06-2001||11:40 PM||||Shhh, you didn't hear this from me, but take the outer door skins off, cut out that support running long ways.Minus 20 lbs.  <BR>Add a steel tube in its place(think rollbar tube) so you wont be killed instantly if you get broadsided.And cut more out of the inside door while you have it apart. And the bumpers can be trimmed some.Inner hood support.every other body bolt.wheel and tire upgrade.tubular suspension parts.Definately A/C.And heater stuff. This won't be driven all the time will it?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000012||DecadenceR||06-07-2001||10:40 AM||||If you're using this strictly offroad, a lot of import racers do this...<BR>Take off the front and rear facias, then remove any energy absorbing material under there. Then get aluminum brackets to hold the shape. <BR>But if you ever get hit or hit anything, there goes your car.||||reg||1
