Z||000016||Toddster||06-08-2001||08:21 PM||||Like anything else it depends on what you are willing to settle for. If the car is exclusively for autocrossing or other racing there is a list of over 100 things that can be cut, ripped, or chucked. If you just want the car to be a little more responsive on the street then the list gets whittled down a bit.<P>Some people above have already made some great suggestions but here are a few more.<P>1) Get the smallest battery you can find that will actually crank your engine over. The battery is the heaviest thing in the car. reducing it's size can shed 20 pounds or more.<P>2) throw out the stereo. Just put a false stereo face plate in.<P>3) cut out the side impact rails in the doors (only if you are going to use the car off-road exclusively)!<P>4) get rid of the entire heater/air system.<P>5) get light weight rims<P>6) toss the cruise<P>7) remove the front and rear steel bumpers and mount the blinker lights on small custom metal brackets instead<P>8) go on a diet!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000017||Frank Sombers||06-08-2001||11:21 PM||||Put helium in your tires.||||reg||1
Z||000018||cadaver||06-09-2001||01:41 PM||||loss the power windows and locks. The power mirrors. The sub system. make sure you take out athe wiring with them.<BR>Install lexan side windows.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000019||Leadfoot||06-11-2001||06:22 PM||||I little late but hey I got time to kill while I am waiting for parts.  <P>This weekend I found the best way to shed a couple of pounds off my 85 SE.  I was easy....all I did was clean the cradle.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||12
